      "category": "history",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Tolsona sits within the expansive Copper River Basin, a lowland shaped by glacial history and surrounded by mountain ranges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tolsona_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community rests at about 2,195 feet (669 meters) above sea level, giving it a moderate elevation for interior Alaska.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tolsona_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tolsona Lake, a shallow glacial lake covering roughly 0.5 square miles, sits in a morainal depression and has no passable inlets or outlets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tolsona_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area supports diverse wildlife, from moose and caribou to brown bears, foxes, and waterfowl, with trout thriving in clear streams.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tolsona_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Tolsona experiences a subarctic continental climate, with winter lows around -10°F and summer highs near 65°F, averaging about 26°F overall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
